This script reads text from the system clipboard, prepends the fixed instruction
"reescreva para deixar mais claro", URL-encodes the result, and opens chat.com in
the default browser with the prompt passed as the ?q= query parameter.

Usage:
    python open-chat-to-rewrite.py

It produces a URL of the form:
    https://chat.com/?q=reescreva+para+deixar+mais+claro%0A%0A<your+clipboard+text>

Functions:
    get_clipboard_content()   Read the clipboard via wl-paste (Wayland).
    build_query()             Prepend the rewrite instruction to the clipboard text.
    build_url()               URL-encode the prompt onto the chat.com base URL.
    main()                    Read clipboard, build the URL, and open the browser.

Dependencies:
    wl-clipboard (provides wl-paste). Install with: sudo apt-get install wl-clipboard
    webbrowser and urllib.parse are part of the Python standard library.

A convenience wrapper, open-chat-to-rewrite.sh, activates the ~/senv virtualenv and
runs the script -- handy for binding to a keyboard shortcut.
